cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use LamiSema in research, please cite it using this metadata."
type: software
title: "LamiSema: Encoding-Aware Nepali PDF Extraction Engine"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-04-18"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/sanjiblamichhane/lamisema"
url: "https://github.com/sanjiblamichhane/lamisema"
abstract: >
  LamiSema is the world's leading structured information extraction system optimized
  for Nepali-language PDFs. It goes beyond character recovery to extract
  structured meaning: tables, sections, and 20+ named entity types covering
  Nepal's administrative, legal, economic, and general-purpose government
  document schemas. The pipeline solves the silent data corruption caused by
  legacy Nepali fonts (Preeti, Kantipur, Sagarmatha) by detecting PDF encoding
  type before extraction and routing each document to the correct strategy.
  The symbolic NLP layer provides rule-based named entity recognition for
  Bikram Sambat dates, NPR currency, organizations, ward codes, districts,
  provinces, land parcel IDs, court references, gazette references, and
  government positions — with no ML model required. Domain-specific extraction
  schemas cover budget documents, land records, gazette notices, court orders,
  economics reports, and general-purpose government documents. Cross-document
  intelligence enables deduplication, version tracking, and entity co-reference
  across document corpora. Designed as the preprocessing layer for the Onto
  swarm intelligence ontology platform.
